# Default-deny build context: `*` excludes everything, and the `!` lines let back in only what a
# build from the repo root needs. Dockerfile's `COPY . .` feeds `cargo build --release -p
# logit-cli`, and Dockerfile.dev copies nothing (the tree is bind-mounted at run time). Hidden
# directories (.git, .claude), target/, and tmp/ never reach the daemon.
#
# Only a build whose context is the repo root reads this file. The Dockerfiles under demo/,
# examples/, tools/, and crates/logit-perf build from their own directory.
#
# A build-time input outside crates/ (a new workspace member, a .cargo/config.toml, an
# include_str! of a file elsewhere) needs its own `!` line, or the release build fails with a
# missing-file error. CI doesn't build the release image, so that failure only shows up in
# script/image and the harnesses that build it.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!rust-toolchain.toml
!crates
